00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:38.398
And on that day I was visiting with
a colleague of mine who works for

00:00:38.398 --> 00:00:43.317
Save the Children Jordan and we got
to meet a friend of mine named Esma.

00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:47.308
We visited Esma trailer, and
we knocked on the wooden door and

00:00:47.308 --> 00:00:51.837
Esma kindly greeted us as she always,
does with such great kindness,

00:00:51.837 --> 00:00:56.593
and we walk in and we sit on the dark
brown carpet on a dark brown cushion with

00:00:56.593 --> 00:00:59.329
the blue flowers all around the trailer.

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:03.446
And we sit and
we drink tea together shy in Arabic,

00:01:03.446 --> 00:01:06.494
the shy that she had prepared for us.

00:01:06.494 --> 00:01:10.946
And as we were drinking our tea Esma was
talking to us about her life in the camper

00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:13.846
life back in Syria and
the great work she's doing in

00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:16.948
the camp suddenly there was
a loud noise around us and so

00:01:16.948 --> 00:01:21.092
the trailer walls started rumbling
it felt like the ground was shaking.

00:01:21.092 --> 00:01:24.526
And finally I looked over
to my colleagues looked

00:01:24.526 --> 00:01:29.313
over to Esma says something going on,
and I said, Yes, just wait.

00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:33.489
And in that moment, 10 children burst
through that wooden door we had come

00:01:33.489 --> 00:01:37.731
through onto the ground and the carpet and
the brown carpet in front of us, and

00:01:37.731 --> 00:01:42.833
